{"schemaVersion":{"minor":3,"patch":0,"major":0},"variants":[{"paths":["\/documentation\/swift\/floatingpoint\/signalingnan"],"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}]}],"sections":[],"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"A signaling NaN (“not a number”)."}],"identifier":{"url":"doc:\/\/com.apple.Swift\/documentation\/Swift\/FloatingPoint\/signalingNaN","interfaceLanguage":"swift"},"hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/com.apple.Swift\/documentation\/Swift","doc:\/\/com.apple.Swift\/documentation\/Swift\/FloatingPoint"]]},"primaryContentSections":[{"kind":"declarations","declarations":[{"tokens":[{"text":"static","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"var","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"signalingNaN","kind":"identifier"},{"text":": ","kind":"text"},{"text":"Self","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":" { ","kind":"text"},{"text":"get","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" }","kind":"text"}],"languages":["swift"],"platforms":["macOS"]}]},{"content":[{"level":2,"type":"heading","anchor":"discussion","text":"Discussion"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"The default IEEE 754 behavior of operations involving a signaling NaN is","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"to raise the Invalid flag in the floating-point environment and return a","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"quiet NaN.","type":"text"}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Operations on types conforming to the ","type":"text"},{"code":"FloatingPoint","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" protocol should","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"support this behavior, but they might also support other options. For","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"example, it would be reasonable to implement alternative operations in","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"which operating on a signaling NaN triggers a runtime error or results","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"in a diagnostic for debugging purposes. Types that implement alternative","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"behaviors for a signaling NaN must document the departure.","type":"text"}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Other than these signaling operations, a signaling NaN behaves in the","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"same manner as a quiet NaN.","type":"text"}]}],"kind":"content"}],"metadata":{"title":"signalingNaN","roleHeading":"Type Property","externalID":"s:SF12signalingNaNxvpZ","role":"symbol","platforms":[{"introducedAt":"8.0","beta":false,"name":"iOS","deprecated":false,"unavailable":false},{"introducedAt":"8.0","beta":false,"name":"iPadOS","deprecated":false,"unavailable":false},{"introducedAt":"13.0","beta":false,"name":"Mac Catalyst","deprecated":false,"unavailable":false},{"introducedAt":"10.10","beta":false,"name":"macOS","deprecated":false,"unavailable":false},{"introducedAt":"9.0","beta":false,"name":"tvOS","deprecated":false,"unavailable":false},{"introducedAt":"1.0","beta":false,"name":"visionOS","deprecated":false,"unavailable":false},{"introducedAt":"2.0","beta":false,"name":"watchOS","deprecated":false,"unavailable":false}],"symbolKind":"property","modules":[{"name":"Swift"}],"fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"static"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"keyword","text":"var"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"signalingNaN"},{"kind":"text","text":": "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"Self"}],"required":true},"kind":"symbol","references":{"doc://com.apple.Swift/documentation/Swift/FloatingPoint/signalingNaN":{"type":"topic","kind":"symbol","title":"signalingNaN","role":"symbol","required":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/com.apple.Swift\/documentation\/Swift\/FloatingPoint\/signalingNaN","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"static"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"keyword","text":"var"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"signalingNaN"},{"kind":"text","text":": "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier"